  "steps": [
    "A driver started `claude --settings <file> --allowedTools \"Bash(ping -c 60 127.0.0.1)\" 'Bash(python3 -c \"import time; time.sleep(60)\")'` in a pseudo-terminal of 160 columns and 50 rows, in a new empty folder that is no git repository, with the person's own settings and plugins in place and no variable of an enclosing Claude Code or Orca session. Every `at` below counts milliseconds from that start.",
    "The settings file gave each of the 33 hook events of the hooks reference (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks, 2026-11-24) one command hook with no matcher. The hook took its `at` as it started and appended the event's JSON to one file, printed nothing, and exited 0.",
    "The driver read the session log, the file each hook event names as `transcript_path`, every 25 ms. A line's `at` is the read that first saw it whole, so a line stood in the file up to 25 ms before its `at`.",
    "Claude Code showed no folder-trust question, so the driver answered none.",
    "At 0.00 s, the driver started the session.",
    "At 1.02 s, the driver learned the session log's path from a hook event.",
    "At 4.63 s, the driver sent the prompt that asks for the numbers 1 to 300, in the words \"Write the numbers from 1 to 300, one per line, and nothing else. Use no tool\".",
    "At 7.72 s, the driver sent Esc during the reply (first interruption).",
    "At 10.54 s, the driver sent the prompt that asks for `ping -c 60 127.0.0.1`, in the words \"Run exactly this one command with the Bash tool, in the foreground, and do nothing else, with no explanation first: <command>\".",
    "At 11.89 s, the driver saw the PreToolUse of the Bash call `ping -c 60 127.0.0.1`.",
    "At 13.90 s, the driver sent Esc during the Bash call (second interruption).",
    "At 14.11 s, the driver began to wait 75 s after the last Esc.",
    "At 89.50 s, the driver typed /exit.",
    "At 90.22 s, the session's process exited.",
    "Two interruptions were recorded. The first Esc stopped the reply while Claude wrote it, with no tool running. The second Esc came 2 s after the PreToolUse of the Bash call `ping -c 60 127.0.0.1`. Before it, the screen showed \"running PreToolUse hooks… 0/2\" for the call, and it showed no output of ping. The person's own settings add PreToolUse hooks beside the recording's. The call's tool result reads \"The user doesn't want to proceed with this tool use\", with `toolDenialKind` `user-rejected`, and the screen then read \"No result recorded for 1 call\": the Esc stopped the call before its command ran. The driver sent no prompt for `python3 -c \"import time; time.sleep(60)\"`, because the ping call reached its PreToolUse.",
    "Paths are replaced by `<transcript_path>`, `<cwd>`, `<scratchpad_dir>` and `<home>`, and each thinking block's signature by `<signature>`. A log line whose type is attachment, api-request-shape, api-request-blob, api-request, session-owner, data-flow-records or cost-state, or whose subtype is stop_hook_summary, carries the person's environment, account or instructions: it stands as its type, its subtype or attachment type, and `redactedCharacters`, the length of the line as written."
  ],
